# Error Handling

Treat network, storage, parsing, and external services as unreliable.

Handle expected failures explicitly.

Provide meaningful application-level errors to the UI instead of exposing infrastructure exceptions directly when appropriate.

Do not silently swallow exceptions.

Every async operation that can fail should have a clear failure path.

Avoid displaying raw technical exceptions to end users.

Preserve diagnostic context for logging while protecting sensitive information.
